# UI styling — Advanced

Enable when rule level includes `advanced`. **Locked base (`ui-styling.mdc`) stays** — extensions only.

## Page transitions

- Route-level transition wrapper (fade/slide 150–250ms)
- Shared `transition-*` tokens; stagger lists sparingly
- Exit animation before unmount when router supports it
- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` → instant or opacity-only

## Infinite scroll

- Intersection Observer sentinel at list foot
- Append skeleton rows while fetching next page
- Dedupe requests; show inline error + retry on failure
- Optional “Load more” button fallback for a11y

## Slideshow / carousel

- Keyboard: arrows, focusable controls
- Touch swipe on mobile
- Pause autoplay on hover/focus and reduced motion
- Lazy-load off-screen slides/images

## Parallax

- Marketing/hero only — not product forms or dashboards
- Transform-based; disable entirely under reduced motion
- Do not harm scroll performance (avoid heavy repaints)

## Charts / graphs

- One chart library per project (record in Profile if chosen)
- Colors from theme tokens only
- Responsive `aspect-video` or min-height container
- Accessible labels / table fallback when feasible

## Bottom toolbar & tabs (mobile)

- Safe-area `pb-safe` for iOS home indicator
- Max 5 primary tab items; badge counts from tokens
- Active state matches primary brand — not random accent per tab

## Premium polish (optional adds)

- Subtle glass/backdrop-blur on marketing panels only
- Micro-interactions on primary CTA (scale/opacity, not bounce spam)
- Section reveal on scroll — once per section, reduced-motion safe

## Do not

- Replace locked Button/Modal/Form primitives with ad-hoc copies
- Add parallax or heavy animation to admin/data tables
- Introduce a second spacing or type scale outside Tailwind theme
